# React component code style

**Default:** generate new feature components using the `frontend/src/components/SiteMenu/` pattern when the task fits (see checklist below).

**If it does not fit:** do not force the SiteMenu layout. Before implementing, tell the user **why not** and which alternative pattern to use (listed below). Then match that pattern instead.

---

## When to use the SiteMenu pattern ✅

Use `SiteMenu/` as the template when **all** of these are true:

| Criterion | SiteMenu example |
|-----------|------------------|
| Self-contained **site chrome** or **feature UI** (nav, tray, panel, toolbar) | `SiteMenu` |
| A few related visual parts (typically 2–4), not a large form/editor | `MenuButton` + `MenuTray` |
| One orchestrator owns UI state (open/closed, active tab) | `isTrayOpen` in `SiteMenu.jsx` |
| Leaf components are mostly presentational | `MenuTray` maps routes to links |
| Feature-specific styles with a shared prefix | `menu_tray`, `menu_button` |
| Optional static config/data separable from React | `routes.js` |

### SiteMenu folder layout (copy this structure)

```
FeatureName/
  index.js              # export { default as FeatureName } from './FeatureName';
  FeatureName.jsx       # orchestrator — state + composition only, NO .css import
  LeafA.jsx             # one default-export component per file
  LeafA.css             # sidecar styles, snake_case, feature prefix
  LeafB.jsx
  LeafB.css
  FeatureIcons.jsx      # optional — named exports for SVGs
  featureData.js        # optional — routes, config, pure logic (not a component)
```

### SiteMenu orchestrator (`SiteMenu.jsx`)

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";
import LeafA from "./LeafA";
import LeafB from "./LeafB";
import getFeatureData from "./featureData";

export default function FeatureName() {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);

  const toggle = () => {
    setIsOpen((prev) => !prev);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <LeafA isOpen={isOpen} getData={getFeatureData} />
      <LeafB isOpen={isOpen} onToggle={toggle} />
    </>
  );
}
```

- State and handlers live **only** in the orchestrator.
- Children receive state + callbacks via props (`isOpen`, `onToggle`).
- Use a fragment `<>...</>` when composing siblings.
- No JSDoc required on simple orchestrators (SiteMenu does not use it).

### SiteMenu leaf component (`MenuTray.jsx`, `MenuButton.jsx`)

```jsx
import "./LeafA.css";

export default function LeafA({ isOpen, getData }) {
  const items = getData(null);

  return (
    <div className={`leaf_a ${isOpen ? "open_leaf_a" : ""}`.trim()}>
      {/* ... */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

- Import sidecar CSS at the top.
- **snake_case** classes prefixed with feature name: `menu_tray`, `menu_tray_nav_item`.
- Open/state modifier classes: `open_menu_tray`, `menu_button_opened_tray`.
- Conditional classes: template string + `.trim()`.
- Interactive elements: `aria-expanded`, `aria-label` where `MenuButton` does.
- External links: `target="_blank"` + `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Buttons: `type="button"` unless submit.

### SiteMenu icons (`MenuIcons.jsx`)

- Named exports (`export function HomeIcon()`), not default.
- SVG: `currentColor`, `aria-hidden="true"`, 20×20 (or 18×14).
- Shared stroke props via a constant (`navIconProps`) when multiple icons match.

### SiteMenu barrel (`index.js`)

```js
export { default as FeatureName } from './FeatureName';
```

Consumers import: `import { SiteMenu } from '../components/SiteMenu'`.

### CSS pairing

- One `.css` per leaf component; orchestrator has **no** CSS file.
- Use tokens from `styles.mdc` (`var(--site-body-bg)`, `--control_min_height`, etc.).
- Breakpoints: `768px` and `1024px` only.

---

## When NOT to use SiteMenu — use these instead

If any **exclusion** below applies, **stop and explain to the user** which row applies and why, then follow that pattern.

| Situation | Why SiteMenu does not fit | Use instead |
|-----------|---------------------------|-------------|
| **Single leaf, no orchestration** | No state to lift; splitting into 3 files adds noise | One file, e.g. `HomeCta/HomeCtaButtons.jsx` — may omit folder orchestrator |
| **Reusable control used across features** | SiteMenu classes (`menu_*`) are feature-specific | `components/ui/SiteControlButton.jsx` — BEM `ui-control`, `ui-control--primary` |
| **Large editor / dashboard / wizard** | Too many subviews, modals, and hooks for one orchestrator + 2 leaves | `PostEditor/`, `CatalogEditor/` — subfolder per concern (`sections/`, modals, hooks colocated) |
| **Global layout shell with portals** | Needs `createPortal`, mount guards, pathname effects | `SiteChrome/SiteChrome.jsx` — effects + portal, not tray/button split |
| **Custom hook only** | Not a component | `useSomething.jsx` in `hooks/` or next to the one consumer |
| **Extending an existing folder** | Consistency beats SiteMenu template | Match the existing folder’s files and naming |
| **Astro-only static markup** | No client state | Prefer `.astro` component; skip React |
| **Third-party or generated code** | Out of project conventions | Keep as-is; do not refactor to SiteMenu |

### Required deviation message (when not fitting)

When skipping SiteMenu, include a short note like:

> **Pattern:** not using SiteMenu layout because [reason from table]. Using `[Alternative]` from `[path]` instead.

---

## Shared rules (all React components)

- **Default export** for main component: `export default function MenuTray`.
- **PascalCase** filenames matching the component name.
- **JSX + JSDoc** for props on non-trivial components (optional on SiteMenu-style leaves).
- Import order: React → siblings → CSS → hooks → lib.
- No TypeScript unless the task explicitly requires it.
- No Tailwind, no anonymous `export default () =>`.
- No `console.log` left in production code.
- Avoid camelCase CSS class names in new feature components.

---

## Quick decision flow

```
New React UI needed?
  └─ Extending PostEditor / Chatbot / existing folder? → match that folder (say so)
  └─ Reusable button/control? → ui/SiteControlButton pattern (say so)
  └─ One-off presentational block? → single .jsx (say so)
  └─ Chrome / tray / toolbar with 2–4 parts + local open state? → SiteMenu pattern ✅
  └─ Large multi-step editor? → PostEditor-style subfolders (say so)
```

